hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1603","Narrated to us Al-Hasan ibn Nasr Al-Mu'arik Al-Misri: Narrated to us Yahya ibn Hassan: Narrated to us 'Abdul-Wahid ibn Ziyad: Narrated to us 'Umarah ibn Al-Qa'qa': On the authority of Abu Zur'ah ibn 'Amr ibn Jarir: On the authority of Abu Hurairah (RA), who said:\n\n\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"," when he stood in the second rak'ah"," would begin recitation with *Alhamdu lillahi Rabbil 'alamin* (All praise is for Allah"," the Lord of all the worlds)"," and he would not pause (before starting the recitation).\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
